# Only the two committed Pi config files ship. Everything else Pi writes into the
# config directory under a local PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR -- auth.json (credentials on
# /login), models-store.json, sessions/, pi-debug.log, trust.json -- must never
# enter the build context; .gitignore is a separate mechanism Docker does not
# read. What does ship is inert: Pi reads it only when PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR points
# at it, and the harness never sets that variable, so the organizers' own Pi
# configuration always wins inside the judged image.
.pi-agent/**
!.pi-agent/models.json
!.pi-agent/settings.json

# Written by the runner. prepareOutput() unlinks a stale copy at run start, so
# this is belt-and-braces; it still should not ride into the image.
result.json
